import json,pathlib
p=pathlib.Path(__file__).parent/'projects'/'episodes.json'; data=json.loads(p.read_text())
lines=[
["Before reliable electrical grids, cities struggled to bring power safely and efficiently to homes and factories.","Nikola Tesla was fascinated by electricity and the possibility of motors without troublesome commutators.","Early power networks faced difficult choices about voltage, distance, and the cost of copper wiring.","Tesla developed polyphase systems that could produce a rotating magnetic field using alternating currents.","That rotating field makes an induction motor work, turning electrical energy into mechanical motion.","In the late eighteen eighties, Tesla patented important parts of his alternating-current motor system.","AC and DC technologies competed, with engineering, economics, and business all shaping the outcome.","George Westinghouse licensed Tesla's patents, helping bring polyphase power systems toward commercial use.","The Chicago World's Fair of eighteen ninety-three became a famous showcase for electric illumination.","Large hydroelectric projects at Niagara Falls helped demonstrate the potential of alternating-current generation and transmission.","Today, induction motors drive pumps, machines, conveyors, and countless other industrial systems.","Tesla did not invent electricity, but his engineering contributions helped shape the electrical world we know."],
["In the eighteenth century, mines needed powerful pumps to keep underground workings free from water.","James Watt began as an instrument maker, with a talent for noticing where machines wasted energy.","Existing steam engines cooled their working cylinders during every cycle, wasting precious heat.","Watt realized steam could be condensed in a separate chamber while the cylinder stayed hot.","This separate condenser dramatically reduced one major source of heat loss in steam engines.","Turning that idea into a reliable machine required years of careful manufacturing and development.","Working with Matthew Boulton, Watt helped bring improved steam engines to industrial customers.","Later developments allowed engines to deliver rotary motion, useful for powering factory machinery.","Factories could increasingly rely on mechanical power rather than only water wheels and animals.","Watt also popularized horsepower as a practical way to describe the work engines could do.","His engines did not create steam power from nothing; they made existing technology more efficient.","The name watt now measures power, a reminder of engineering's role in the industrial revolution."],
["Michael Faraday began his working life binding books, not studying at an elite university.","He read the scientific volumes that passed through the shop and taught himself relentlessly.","After attending Humphry Davy's lectures, Faraday found an opportunity at the Royal Institution.","In the laboratory, careful experiments became his greatest tool for understanding electricity and magnetism.","In eighteen twenty-one, he demonstrated electromagnetic rotation, an early principle behind electric motors.","Faraday imagined magnetic effects as patterns of force extending through the space around magnets.","In eighteen thirty-one, his experiments revealed how changing magnetism could produce an electric current.","This is electromagnetic induction: a changing magnetic field can generate an electric voltage.","That principle became fundamental to electrical generators, transformers, and much of modern power engineering.","Faraday shared science with public audiences and valued clear demonstrations over grand claims.","Electric motors in today's robots still depend on the interaction of currents and magnetic fields.","His discoveries helped connect simple laboratory experiments to the electrical technologies surrounding us."],
["Thomas Edison is often remembered for the light bulb, but the real story is bigger.","As a young inventor, Edison gained experience with telegraphy and practical electrical problems.","At Menlo Park, he created an organized laboratory where experiments could be repeated and improved.","Edison's inventions depended on teams of skilled assistants, machinists, and researchers working together.","They tested many materials to develop incandescent lamps that could work reliably in practice.","A useful lighting system needed generators, cables, switches, meters, and distribution, not just bulbs.","Public demonstrations helped convince people that electric lighting could become an everyday service.","Early power stations showed how invention had to become infrastructure before it could change cities.","Edison also developed the phonograph, an extraordinary early technology for recording and reproducing sound.","His career shows the value of prototyping, testing, documentation, and organized research.","Modern engineering laboratories continue to combine specialized teams with iterative experimentation.","Edison did not invent the first light bulb; he helped make electric lighting commercially practical."],
["Centuries before modern engineering software, Leonardo da Vinci studied the mechanics of the world.","As an apprentice in Renaissance Italy, he learned to observe, draw, and construct.","His notebooks mixed questions, sketches, and ideas about machines, nature, and human anatomy.","He investigated gears, bearings, friction, and the transmission of motion between components.","Lifting devices and cranes fascinated him because they could multiply human effort.","Leonardo also watched water move, drawing currents, turbulence, and flowing patterns.","He imagined flying machines inspired by birds, long before powered flight became practical.","Most of these flight concepts were not built or successfully flown in his lifetime.","His anatomical studies reveal the same habit: observe carefully, then record structures precisely.","He sketched bridges and mechanical systems, exploring how forces pass through structures.","Leonardo's work crossed boundaries between art, science, geometry, and engineering design.","His greatest legacy may be curiosity: ask how something works, then investigate it rigorously."]]
for ep, narr in zip(data,lines):
 for scene,line in zip(ep['scenes'],narr):scene['narration']=line
p.write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False))
